    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/05/brooks-ghost-max-3-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: DNA Loft v3 feels soft and compliant with strong impact absorption, and the heel bevel plus early forefoot rocker produce smooth transitions despite a stiff forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is mostly non-responsive with limited snappiness; there is only a slight bounce increase after break-in, so it performs best at easy/slower paces.",
        "Stability: Stable-neutral ride is a clear strength, driven by high torsional rigidity (wide base, stiff platform, guidance geometry), a stiff padded heel counter, and supportive sidewalls/lateral structure.",
        "Durability: Outsole and overall build are highly durable, with extensive rubber showing minimal wear (no notable outsole dent after ~30 miles) and above-average longevity expected from upper/midsole materials."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/11/brooks-ghost-max-3-multi-tester-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning is protective and forgiving with strong vibration dampening, but the underfoot feel is muted/traditional and slightly firm rather than plush-max; the 39 mm heel / 33 mm forefoot setup feels soft enough without being very soft.",
        "Responsiveness is limited: the ride is described as bland, not very spritely, with low bounce/energy return and only moderate snappiness from the GlideRoll rocker.",
        "Stability is a key strength due to the very wide platform (about 114 mm heel / 120 mm forefoot) and secure lockdown, giving solid lateral support for neutral to mild stability needs; torsional rigidity and heel-counter stiffness are not explicitly quantified.",
        "Durability looks excellent: robust, high-coverage outsole rubber and workhorse construction, with roughly 150 miles reported and hardly any outsole wear, indicating strong long-term material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/brooks-ghost-max-3-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: DNA Loft v3 is reported as slightly softer/plusher than Ghost Max 2 (after a short break-in), with a very comfortable underfoot feel and padded heel/tongue around a high 39/33 mm stack for impact protection.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is described as a bit bouncier, smoother, and more fluid than v2 while retaining moderate daily-trainer responsiveness, but it is not especially snappy or \"fun\" versus faster options.",
        "Stability: A broad/wide base and secure upper give general support, but the fit is notably roomy in both heel and forefoot, and one reviewer noted medial roll-in/stability issues on a weaker side despite the wide platform.",
        "Durability: No clear long-term outsole wear or upper/material longevity findings are provided in this review text."
      ]
    }
